# Tempo ride - the new track arrives at the old one's speed and accelerates into its own.
#
# Where sync-blend hides the change, this one uses it. The old track is gone by the quarter
# mark, so the whole rest of the move is the new one alone, climbing from a borrowed tempo
# to the one it was made at. On records that are close in speed it reads as a lift; on ones
# that are far apart the player refuses to stretch at all and this is simply a fast fade.

name    Tempo ride
note    arrives at the old tempo and climbs into its own
bars    16
align   beat
power   free

lane out gain
    bar 0     1.0    power-down
    bar 4     0.0    hold
    bar 16    0.0    hold

lane in gain
    bar 0     0.0    power-up
    bar 4     1.0    hold
    bar 16    1.0    hold

# The climb is the point, so it is long and even rather than hidden.
lane in tempo
    bar 0     0.0    hold
    bar 4     0.0    linear
    bar 16    1.0    hold

# It opens up as it speeds up.
lane in lowpass
    bar 0    4000    smooth
    bar 10  16000    smooth
    bar 12      0    hold
    bar 16      0    hold
